      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(telegram): catch unhandled rejections in webhook and ingress worker shutdown",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes three channel reliability bugs in the Telegram plugin where shutdown paths can produce unhandled promise rejections (Node.js terminates the process by default) or skip owned cleanup:\n\n1. **Webhook shutdown `bot.stop()` rejection**: if `bot.stop()` rejected, the rejection was unhandled (`void shutdown()`), and owned cleanup—`closeTransportOnce()`, `status.noteWebhookStop()`, `stopDiagnosticHeartbeat()`—was silently skipped, leaking sockets and leaving stale status.\n2. **Ingress worker stop not idempotent**: calling `stop()` twice created a second `stop` postMessage and a second 15s terminate timer. If `worker.terminate()` rejected, the rejection was unhandled.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- **Webhook**: wrap `bot.stop()` in `try/finally` so cleanup always runs even through rejection. The caller-side `.catch()` routes the error to `runtime.error` but the `finally` block guarantees transport close, status update, and diagnostics stop independent of the `bot.stop()` outcome.\n- **Ingress worker**: guard `stop()` with a shared `stopPromise` for idempotency (same promise on repeated calls), catch `postMessage` errors for already-terminated workers, and catch `worker.terminate()` rejections.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo more unhandled rejection crashes or socket leaks during Telegram channel restart or shutdown. Cleanup (transport close, status, diagnostics) always completes even if `bot.stop()` fails.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Forward Proof — All Tests Pass\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs \\\n  extensions/telegram/src/webhook.test.ts \\\n  extensions/telegram/src/telegram-ingress-worker.test.ts -- --run\n```\n\n```\n Test Files  2 passed (2)\n      Tests  38 passed (38)\n   Duration  22.71s\n```\n\n### Negative Control — Bug Reproduction on origin/main\n\n```bash\ngit checkout origin/main -- extensions/telegram/src/telegram-ingress-worker.ts extensions/telegram/src/webhook.ts\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/telegram/src/telegram-ingress-worker.test.ts extensions/telegram/src/webhook.test.ts -- --run\n```\n\n**Result: ❌ FAILED — 2 test files failed**\n\n```\n FAIL  extensions/telegram/src/telegram-ingress-worker.test.ts > createTelegramIngressWorker stop > is idempotent\nAssertionError: expected Promise{…} to be Promise{…} // Object.is equality\n\n FAIL  extensions/telegram/src/webhook.test.ts > startTelegramWebhook > does not leak unhandled rejections\nAssertionError: expected \"vi.fn()\" to be called at least once\n\n Test Files  2 failed (2)\n      Tests  2 failed | 36 passed (38)\n```\n\n**Restore fixes → ✅ PASSED (38/38 tests)**\n\n### Quantified Impact\n\n| Metric | Before Fix | After Fix |\n|--------|-----------|-----------|\n| Unhandled rejections on shutdown | 2 paths | 0 paths |\n| Socket leak risk | Yes (transport not closed) | No (always closed in finally) |\n| Stop idempotency | No (distinct promises) | Yes (shared stopPromise) |\n| Cleanup completion guarantee | Conditional on bot.stop() success | Unconditional (finally block) |\n| Test failures on origin/main | 2 files, 2 tests | 0 files, 0 tests |\n\n### Changes\n\n- `extensions/telegram/src/webhook.ts:1015-1025`: wrap `bot.stop()` in `try/finally` so cleanup runs unconditionally\n- `extensions/telegram/src/webhook.test.ts`: assert `transportCloseSpies[0]` called once through the finally block even when `bot.stop()` rejects\n- `extensions/telegram/src/telegram-ingress-worker.ts:109-152`: idempotent `stop()` with shared stop promise, catch `postMessage` and `terminate` errors\n- `extensions/telegram/src/telegram-ingress-worker.test.ts`: tests for stop idempotency and terminate rejection handling\n\n---\n\n**Mark as AI-assisted**\n\n",
        "branch": "fix/channel-bugs-batch-2026-07-06",
